      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ULTRASONIC (4) improved sharply when second at Wagga and the bump passing the 200m adds merit. Nearing a peak now and gets the blinkers applied. Bold showing anticipated. MISS MAYHEM (8) was well beaten on debut at Bendigo after beginning slowly and racing keenly but did make some late inroads. Her Flemington trial work before that gives her enough upside to be taken seriously with that run out of the way. NOT GUILTY (3) brings the clearest exposed form, having resumed with a brave second at Gundagai on heavy ground after racing wide throughout. The move from 1000m to 1200m is the main question, but he drops to 57.5kg and sets the standard if he repeats that effort. ARTIE'S GAL (5) is an unknown but her Gundagai trial placing and solid family background make her a genuine debut threat rather than a speculative runner. McDougall's booking is a good sign too. DEI MIRACOLI (2) has jumped out well prior to his debut and is drawn cosy. Keeping safe.",
